<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trans-Ecuadorian Oil Pipeline System</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1972">1972</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as SOTE</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Trans-Ecuadorian Oil Pipeline System is the main oil pipeline of Ecuador, running about 500 kilometres from Lago Agrio in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> across the Andes to the Pacific port of Esmeraldas. Opened in 1972, it made oil Ecuador's leading export and the main source of state revenue. Ecuador joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opec">OPEC</a> the following year.</p></div>
